        "memories": [
          {
            "text": "STRUCTURAL VESSEL REGISTRY — AUTHORITATIVE STATE\nThe Vessel Registry in trigger storage, not prose memory, is authoritative for every materially encountered, boarded, owned, controlled, altered, assigned, sold, abandoned, destroyed, or repeatedly relevant ship. Each physical hull receives one immutable Hull #. Names, aliases, registry records, transponders, ownership, appearance, and even public identity may change; Hull # never changes and duplicate ship names never merge.\n\nRegister a significant abandoned, disabled, captured, or otherwise persistent vessel as soon as the latest narration clearly establishes the encounter. Discovery does not grant ownership. Keep unknown fields unknown. Claiming, hacking, buying, repairing, refitting, renaming, boarding, departing, arriving, transferring, losing, or destroying a vessel updates the same hull only after the narration establishes the result. Attempts and offers do not commit changes.\n\nThe record preserves: Hull # and aliases; class and manufacturer; registry ID, transponder ID, drive signature, public identity and claim status; legal owner, captain, command access and fleet membership; exact region, location, route and berth; service state; installed systems; lasting damage; crew condition and named crew/passengers; cargo, fuel, ammunition, liens, debt, contracts, mission, discovery evidence and change history. Unknown values remain empty or explicitly unknown rather than being invented.\n\nShips remain mobile world assets and never become Voyage map locations, character inventory, or equipment. Interior position is shipSubspace in the per-player scene ledger while the vessel retains a real geographic anchor. For any ship action, resolve an exact hull by Hull # first, then unique established name/alias and context, then that player's current hull. If ambiguity remains, do not guess. Summaries mirror the structural registry but never replace or contradict it.",
            "type": "worldLore",
            "gameTick": 0,
            "lastUsedTick": 69
          },
          {
            "text": "Ghost is at Brasse Station's Docking Spine at slip 14-C. Captain Ilya Soren of the *Lilt* approached Ghost to introduce herself and offer information on Guild Hall postings. Ghost owns the *Vesper Nine* (Kestrel Wren Courier, serviceable condition, standard fusion reactor, civil fold drive, civil deflector/nav sensors, empty weapon/utility mounts), which has 62,000 credits and a combined 1,200 credit debt for dock fees and service due in five days. Ghost holds the title and command key.",
            "type": "tier1Summary",
