    {
      "userId": "0",
      "username": "Narrator",
      "text": "Based on what's established in the story so far, here's what's known about the **Orison Combine freighter**:\n\n**What Pike told you:**\n- There's an **Orison Combine hull** in the Ninefold debris field.\n- Word is she was carrying **cybernetics that aren't on any manifest** — unmanifested cargo.\n- The **Guild's official sweep team won't be out for another few days**, which is why there's a window before they log the wreck and claim salvage rights.\n- Pike wants what's in the cargo bay before that happens.\n\n**Pike's knowledge and motivations (the record behind his offer):**\n- Pike is currently **dodging a debt to a local fuel supplier** after a prior salvage run near the Ninefold corridor turned up only scrap.\n- He already knew the \"debris field\" in the Guild posting is actually the **remains of this Orison Combine freighter** — that's why he flagged the run in the first place.\n- He's looking for a pilot with a **clean signature** to ferry him out so he can snag the high-value cargo **before the Guild's official sweep teams** arrive.\n- He's not a pirate, just broke and willing to play loose with salvage rights.\n\n**What's not clearly established:**\n- No details in the record about the freighter's class, tonnage, crew, fate (what destroyed it), or what the cybernetics are specifically meant to be — those haven't been filled in yet.\n\nSo one fact is worth treating carefully: Pike told you he knows the field, but he only just now revealed the Orison Combine connection when pressed. Whether the \"unmanifested cybernetics\" being there is the truth or just what he's telling you remains open — his hidden record describes it as the cargo he's chasing.\n\nWant me to audit anything else — the *Lilt*, the Guild contract, the project ledger?",
