    "Map Scale and Travel": {
      "text": "The Open Meridian realm is an intergalactic overview. Its regions are galaxies and its location pins are useful system-scale anchors, not every star. Major authored planets can open a separate surface realm; smaller worlds remain complex locations with landing, settlement, wilderness, and orbital areas. Passing ships, temporary camps, anomalies, wrecks, and minor stations stay narrative encounters until play makes them persistent.\n\nOrdinary travel time depends on distance, ship, corridor, traffic, and weather. Local docking can take minutes to hours; travel inside a system hours to days; a charted fold passage hours to several days; sparse multi-leg travel days to weeks. Each map region occupies one compact tile-grid coordinate; location pins use coordinates inside their own region. Compress repetitive cruise only after departure, costs, cargo needs, and meaningful route choices are settled. A takeoff is departure, not instant arrival. Do not add an encounter merely because time passed.",
