      "text": "Authored reactor systems. A compatible system becomes part of a named vessel only after purchase or recovery, delivery, yard access, installation, integration, and any required trial or certification. Installed systems belong in the vessel ledger, never character inventory or equipment slots.\n\nCompact Fusion Reactor — A common low-maintenance reactor for skiffs, shuttles, and light civilian craft. Typical price 22,000 credits before installation.\nCommercial Fusion Stack — A serviceable modular power stack for freighters, cutters, and medium working ships. Typical price 180,000 credits before installation.\nHigh-Flux Military Reactor — A tightly controlled reactor built for rapid weapon, shield, and drive load changes. Typical price 1,800,000 credits before installation.\nKethari Redundant Core — Four isolated reactor blocks that can be serviced or sacrificed independently during damage. Typical price 2,200,000 credits before installation.\nVector Adaptive Power Lattice — A software-defined power lattice that shifts cleanly between laboratories, drones, shields, and propulsion. Typical price 2,600,000 credits before installation.",
