    "Ship Systems — Drive": {
      "text": "Authored drive systems. A compatible system becomes part of a named vessel only after purchase or recovery, delivery, yard access, installation, integration, and any required trial or certification. Installed systems belong in the vessel ledger, never character inventory or equipment slots.\n\nCivil Fold Drive — A certified fold drive for charted corridors, conservative emergence, and ordinary commercial schedules. Typical price 95,000 credits before installation.\nCourier Fold Drive — A fast-cycling drive for small ships that trades cargo volume and service life for schedule speed. Typical price 420,000 credits before installation.\nLong-Range Fold Drive — An efficient drive with expanded reserve and cooling for sparse routes and exploration. Typical price 1,200,000 credits before installation.\nMilitary Pursuit Drive — A high-thrust fold and normal-space package built for repeated combat maneuver and pursuit. Typical price 3,800,000 credits before installation.\nSilent-Entry Drive — An expensive drive and thermal package that reduces the emissions of a carefully planned emergence. Typical price 6,500,000 credits before installation.",
