    "Ship Systems — Weapon Hardpoint": {
      "text": "Authored weapon hardpoint systems. A compatible system becomes part of a named vessel only after purchase or recovery, delivery, yard access, installation, integration, and any required trial or certification. Installed systems belong in the vessel ledger, never character inventory or equipment slots.\n\nCoilgun Turret — A reliable ship turret firing dense magnetic projectiles; damage type: ballistic. Typical price 210,000 credits before installation.\nLaser Point-Defense Cluster — Fast-tracking defensive lasers for missiles, debris, drones, and exposed small craft; damage type: thermal. Typical price 340,000 credits before installation.\nPlasma Battery — A short-to-medium-range ship battery with severe heat and power demand; damage type: plasma. Typical price 780,000 credits before installation.\nMissile Rack — A configurable rack for guided ship missiles; ammunition and warhead determine final damage type. Typical price 460,000 credits before installation.\nHeavy Rail Battery — A capital-scale kinetic battery requiring long firing geometry and major structural support; damage type: ballistic. Typical price 8,500,000 credits before installation.\nIon Disruptor — A specialized emitter intended to overload exposed electrical and control systems; damage type: electrical. Typical price 1,400,000 credits before installation.\nBoarding Pod Rack — Launch hardware for armored personnel pods and breaching attachments rather than direct hull damage. Typical price 620,000 credits before installation.\nMining Lance — An industrial beam and cutter mount for breaking asteroid or surface material; damage type: thermal. Typical price 520,000 credits before installation.\nElectronic-Warfare Emitter — A directional transmitter array for jamming, spoofing, and network attack against reachable systems; damage type: digital. Typical price 2,400,000 credits before installation.\nRescue Tractor Array — A precise gravitic and tether system for stabilizing damaged craft, pod