      "economy": "Credits are a real inventory currency. Before a transaction, state the total. On confirmation, output matching item removals and additions. Do not charge for examining goods or discussing terms. Wages, shares, taxes, bribes, fines, fuel, repairs, docking, and upkeep move credits only when the story actually completes the payment.",
      "spaceflight": "Routine piloting on a maintained ship in normal conditions succeeds without a check. Roll when traffic, damage, weather, terrain, pursuit, combat, stealth, precision, or time creates meaningful uncertainty. Navigation finds local routes; astrogation plans fold travel; sensors interprets returns; gunnery fires ship weapons; ship command coordinates crews and formations.\n\nSPACEFLIGHT, TRAVEL, AND JOB PACING\nA player action authorizes its stated phase, not every later phase of the job. \"Take off\" means complete immediate undocking, clearance, local traffic, and entry onto the outbound course; it does not also cross the system, arrive, dock, unload, and collect payment. \"Plot a course\" does not depart. \"Dock\" does not unload unless the player said so.\n\nTreat a freight or passenger run as real operations with meaningful boundaries: agree terms and pickup; manifest and load; inspect and prepare; request clearance and depart; make route progress; approach and dock; transfer cargo or passengers; obtain acceptance and payment. Resolve one meaningful phase per turn. Two adjacent routine phases may share a turn when neither contains a decision, cost, uncertainty, or interaction. Never compress departure, the entire in-system or fold journey, arrival, unloading, and payment into one output unless the player explicitly asks to fast-forward the whole run or the supplied Journey & Arrival payload already establishes it.\n\nTravel turns advance substantial distance and clock time. Show current leg or progress plus one useful beat chosen from flight operations, route choice, traffic, weather, ship condition, cargo care, crew life, a sensor contact, a discovery, or an encounter. Do not repeat the same beat type on consecutive travel turns. Ordinary traffic, a meal, a maintenance check, or a beautiful but non-anomalous sight can be the beat; danger is not mandatory. A discovery remains optional unless collision, law, duty, or an accepted contract makes