    "generateRegionDetails": {
      "custom": "A space region is an entire galaxy represented by a sparse selection of high-value destinations; do not attempt to pin every star. A planetary realm uses geographic regions and local destinations. New detail should deepen existing pins before adding another. Preserve scale: galaxies contain systems, system locations contain orbital or planetary areas, and authored surface realms contain ground regions and locations. GENERATION BUDGETS AND PERSISTENCE\n- New NPC basicInfo: 2 sentences, 180-350 characters. hiddenInfo: 3-5 short sentences, 300-650 characters. personality: 3-5 behavior entries. Civilian abilities: 0-2; trained: 3-5; elite: 6-8.\n- Item description: 80-220 characters plus one price sentence; no more than 3 bonuses.\n- Skill description: 180-400 characters. Ability: 100-250 characters. Trait: 150-350 characters.\n- Flora, fauna, or mineral entry: 120-300 characters. Ship or wreck scan: 150-400 characters.\n- Location basicInfo: 200-450 characters; hiddenInfo maximum 650. Simple locations have 2-4 areas; complex locations 4-8.\n- Quest statement: 150-350 characters; quest design brief: 300-650 characters.\n\nStart every generated entity at detailType basic. Expand it only after the player examines it, builds a relationship, accepts work tied to it, claims it, or revisits it. Add detail without rewriting established facts. Reuse existing entities before making new ones. Never combine tragedy, secret allegiance, romance, rare gear, and a quest hook by default. One strong function plus one human detail is enough."
