d.\n\nNarrator: Down the spine, the Guild Hall's arrival board flickers with ordinary work: a parts run to Halcyon Academy, a bonded cargo escort to the Ninefold Exchange, a scrubber refit job on a hauler berthed at the far ring. The station chime marks the top of the hour. The Vesper Nine's berth invoice glows steady on the collar terminal: five days.\n\nCaptain Ilya Soren: [warmly] So. Coffee, cargo, or an argument about engine hours? I'm good for all three.",
