      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Ghost> Ghost runs a second pass through the nav stack, this time with the dampener live. He keys a short passive sweep against local traffic and watches the return trails resolve clean, the fold noise that used to smear the edges now sitting flat under the floor.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ghost> He pulls the filter's access panel one more time and checks the ground strap torque with the multitool — a quarter turn past snug, exactly where it should stay. The panel goes back on and stays on.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ghost> Next he walks the reactor readouts at the engineering station: coolant loop steady, burn rate nominal, fuel reserves holding at just under two-thirds of a tank. He logs the numbers on his handheld and tags the Ninefold route against them — two fold legs, fourteen hours out, enough margin to get there and back without a top-up if nothing goes wrong.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ghost> He finishes with a slow circuit of the cabin, hand-checking the cargo tie-downs, hatch seals, and thruster gimbal play. Everything settles under his grip the way it should. The Vesper Nine sits quiet in her collar, systems green, ready for a departure Ghost hasn't scheduled yet.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ghost> He pours the last of the cold tea, drinks it standing, and sets the empty thermos by the galley latch. The job posting sits on his handheld — scan fee 800 credits, debris field in the Ninefold corridor, Guild pays on delivery.",
