      "storyMessage": "Ghost: [skeptically] A freighter? Fuck me. Let's talk on my ship. More privacy.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Pike> Pike nods once and falls into step, boots ringing on the deck plating as he heads for slip 14-C without waiting for a second invitation.\n\nPike: [flatly] Lead the way.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ghost> Ghost thumbs the collar hatch open and ducks through. Pike follows, ducking his head under the frame, and plants his magnetic boots wide in the cabin, one hand braced on the tie-down rail as his eyes sweep the nav stack — the new dampener housing, the inline filter, the torque-marked ground strap.\n\nPike: [gravelly] Huh. Somebody's already done work on your receiver. Dampener and a filter, by the look of it.\n\nPike: [calmly] Good. Means fold noise out there won't eat your returns. That corridor's dirty enough that most pilots fly it half-blind.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Pike> He settles a hip against the galley counter, unhurried, and pulls a folded scrap of printout from his jumpsuit pocket — a grainy long-range frame of the debris field, one mass circled in grease pencil.\n\nPike: [flatly] There she is. Orison Combine hull, dead center of the field. She's mostly intact — spine broke, but the cargo bay held. That's where the cybernetics are sitting, still crated.\n\nPike: [bluntly] So here's the shape of it. You fly me out, run your scan for the Guild like the posting says — that part's clean, that part's yours. While your sensors are doing the official work, I'm outside in a suit cutting into the bay. We split whatever comes out of it, even, and you get first pick. Nobody files anything, nobody signs anything.\n\nPike: [gravelly] Your ship, your rules. But that's the deal on the table.",
