      "storyParagraphs": [
        "Ghost: I'll make sure we get your crates on my ship first. While you load what you want to keep or sell, I'll be working the freighter and see what can be done about her.",
        "Pike: [calmly] Once we hit the Exchange, I'll square away my gear and get suited up. You get us positioned close and handle the scan — I'll do the EVA and find those crates. We pull what fits, you file the claim, and we're off before anyone else gets curious.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Ghost> Ghost rolls the Vesper Nine onto the outbound lane and opens the throttle, the courier's fusion drive settling into a steady burn as Brasse Station shrinks behind them.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Pike> Pike braces in the cockpit doorway, watching the traffic thin out to scattered transponder blips as the first fold corridor marker comes up on the nav plot.",
        "Pike: [gravelly] First leg's the short one. Fourteen hours total, both folds, if the corridor's behaving. With that dampener of yours, you should read it clean.",
        "Narrator: <hit:encounter:grak-hail> Thirteen kilometers out, a hardlight marker blinks on the passive display — a lone figure in a heavy hardsuit, EVA against a mangled slab of orbital debris, torch sparks drifting off the work site. Short-range hail crackles through.",
        "Grak: [booming cheerfully] Vessel off Brasse! Grak of the Kethari, working the wire line here. You two look like honest scavs — I've got a civilian shield generator, slightly dinged but full function, and I'd trade it for fresh water canisters and a signal booster. Interested?",
        "Pike: [gravelly] Kethari out here alone, stripping wiring by hand. That's either dedication or desperation.",
        "Ghost: [flatly] What's the news out here, Grak? Any reason the corridors are playing nice or not?",
        "Grak: [cheerfully] Ah, you ask the right question! The debris fields have been shifting this past week — old collision wreckage drifting out of the marked lanes. If you're bound for the Kestrel Ring Shipyards, watch your plot — the field edge has crept toward the corridor mouth. Fold noise is worse than usual. Good thing for you, my generator would help with that. So — water and a booster, yes?"
      ],
