        "Ghost": "Bring the Vesper Nine to a halt and use the ship's sensors to scan the area around Grak. Ghost aims to verify the Kethari's claims about the shifting debris and fold noise, checking the passive display for any unexpected wreckage or signs of other scavengers lingering near the corridor entrance. Then Agree to the trade to secure the shield generator.\nGhost opens a comms channel and says, \"I can do the water and the booster. Bring the generator alongside and we'll swap.\" He then checks the inventory for the specific supplies and prepares the airlock for a quick exchange."
      },
      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Ghost> Ghost eases the throttle to null and the Vesper Nine holds station thirteen kilometers off Grak's work site. He lets the passive display build a picture: the debris slab Grak is tethered to, a scatter of collision fragments drifting slow, and the corridor mouth beyond — its field edge pushed noticeably inward from the charted line.\n\nGhost: [flatly] I can do the water and the booster. Bring the generator alongside and we'll swap.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ghost> The scan confirms Grak's story — old wreckage has crept across the marked lane edge, and fold noise readings near the corridor mouth run hotter than the chart baseline. No other transponders linger in the area. Just the Kethari, his sled, and the wire line.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Pike> Pike steps back into the galley and pops the supply locker, rummaging through the stores.\n\nPike: [gravelly] I'll pull what we've got. How many canisters are we giving up — and do we even have a booster to spare?\n\nNarrator: <focus:Pike> He holds up two full water canisters and, after a dig behind the spare parts bin, a standard-band signal booster still in its wrap.\n\nPike: [calmly] Two canisters and a standard-band booster. That fair trade for a dinged generator, I'd say.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Grak> Grak detaches the shield generator from his work sled with two of his four arms and pushes off toward the courier, tether paying out behind him.\n\nGrak: [booming cheerfully] Smart move stopping! Generator's rated for courier-class deflectors — took a scrape on the casing but the coil's intact, I tested it myself. You bring the water canisters to the airlock and I'll float the unit over. Booster too, standard signal band?\n\nGhost: [flatly] Two canisters and a standard-band booster. That's what you get.\n\nGrak: [laughing] Ha! Honest man. Bring them to your airlock — I'll meet you at the hatch.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ghost> Ghost cycles the airlock and passes the canisters and booster out to Grak's gloved hands. In exchange, the shield generator drifts across — a squat cylinder the size of a cargo drum, casing scraped along one flank but the mounting frame sound.\n\nGrak: [cheerfully] Good doing business with you, big man. Mind the field edge on your way in — and if you pass this way again, Grak's always trading.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ghost> Ghost hauls the generator inside by its frame and sets it down in the cargo bay, sealing the airlock behind him. The unit's casing scuff is cosmetic; the coil housing reads intact when he thumbs the test stud.",
