      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Ghost> Ghost walks the hold one last time — cradle strapped, five bins locked, tooling crate padded — then releases the magnetic grapple and eases the Vesper Nine clear of the Carrow's sheared spine.\n\nPike: [gravelly] Remaining bins and crates are strapped tight in bay three. Door's sealed. Drop me wherever's cleanest for the split and I'll walk my share into a buyer.\n\nGhost: [flatly] Will do. Sending Ilya the real numbers now.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ghost> Ghost keys a message to Ilya Soren as the Vesper Nine turns out of the debris field.\n\nGhost: [flatly] We talk about 800 tons, Ilya. I only took a small part of it — my ship can't carry that much. So it's more than just some bins. Cargo's officially claimed and legally mine, so no issues there. About the share — how much percentage do you want so it's worth the work?\n\nIlya Soren: [dryly] Eight hundred tonnes and you fly a Wren. Of course you do. Ten percent of whatever my bins and crates fetch, and I'll run the second load. Send me the claim ID so I can verify before I burn fuel.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Pike> Pike settles into the second seat and plots a short hop toward a quiet Exchange-adjacent berth for his drop.\n\nPike: [gravelly] Twenty klicks ahead there's a maintenance collar nobody watches. That works for me.\n\nNarrator: Twenty kilometers out, the hardened signal filter picks up a distress squawk on the bounty-standard frequency before the visuals resolve.\n\nNarrator: <arrival> A sleek private courier in chrome and glass hangs dead in the dark, its fold corridor cut off by a localized interdiction field. Two interceptor drones circle it in tight orbits while two modified salvage skiffs hold position against its airlock, torches flaring against the hull. Four lifesigns ride the skiffs.\n\nPike: [gravelly] Pirates burning through that airlock. Four crew, two skiffs, two drones. That courier's squawking for any authorized pilot willing to drive them off and escort them out — bounty-standard pay.\n\nGhost: [flatly] Bounty-standard. That could cover Ilya's fuel and then some.\n\nPike: [gravelly] Your call, pilot. We're loaded near the wire — a hard burn or a shield hit changes the math.",
