        "Ghost": "I send both drones praise of good work, promising repairs and service once we reach a harbor. Then i connect to the yacht and claim ownership of it on legal channels before running checks on it and have it follow me."
      },
      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Ghost> Ghost sends a short commendation down both locked channels — good work, repairs and service at the next harbor — and both drones' oculars pulse green in acknowledgment before settling back into escort formation.\n\nPike: [gravelly] Look at those sensor returns. Luxury hull, high-end finishes, steward-grade systems — that's a goldmine on rails. Let's lock it down before some other vulture sniffs the same signal.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ghost> Ghost jacks into the yacht's registry interface and runs the ownership transfer through the open civil channels — clean credentials, delinquent owner flag, no counter-claims. The registry accepts the filing, but the yacht's hardened steward core balks at his intrusion deck, forcing him to fall back on the legal handshake rather than a root rewrite.\n\nAutomated Steward: [formally] Ownership recognized. Welcome aboard, Captain Ghost. All systems are standing by for your commands.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Automated Steward> The steward's voice carries a faint synthetic warmth as it initiates a full interior diagnostic, cabin lights flickering on deck by deck aboard the drifting yacht.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ghost> Ghost runs his checks — drive signature intact, transponder clean but flagged for re-registration at a port office, fuel cell at forty percent, no hull breaches. The yacht answers his follow command and eases out of its drift, thrusters flaring as it falls into formation behind the Vesper Nine.\n\nPike: [gravelly, low whistle] She follows like a show dog. Congratulations, Captain — you just doubled your convoy. Now let's get out of this field before the skiffs reboot or the Guild sweep shows up asking questions.",
