      "storyMessage": "Automated Steward: [calmly] Of course, Captain. Transmitting the verified certificate of ownership transfer to your personal link now, along with a full system summary.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Automated Steward> A data packet arrives on Ghost's board: a registry-stamped certificate bearing the transfer filing ID, plus the yacht's status — hull integrity nominal, fuel cell at forty percent, life support green, cold galley stocked, no passengers, drive signature unchanged and pending re-registration at a port office.\n\nAutomated Steward: [formally] To confirm, Captain: you hold legal title and command authority. I remain at your disposal for scheduling, maintenance tracking, and flight operations. I have also logged a maintenance ledger of accrued costs from my period of neglect — for your records, not as a demand.\n\nPike: [gravelly] Good, it's official. Now listen — we're sitting in a debris pocket with two gutted skiffs, a Guild claim on the Carrow, and a yacht that needs its papers stamped. Set a course for the nearest safe port, get that re-registration done, and lock in the cargo before the sweep teams start sniffing around.\n\nPike: [gravelly] Brasse is closest, but it's also busy. Your call where we land — just pick somewhere before this window closes.",
