      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Ghost> Ghost eases the Vesper Nine out of the debris pocket, both drones holding escort formation, the chrome yacht trailing behind on follow. He sets course for the transfer point Pike named — a bare rendezvous beacon off the maintenance collar where Pike can catch a shuttle back toward Brasse.\n\nPike: [gravelly] Before you drop me — checked the numbers. That load's heavy. Biosynths, five bins, tooling crate, cradle. She'll fly slower back to Brasse, burn more. If you're towing that yacht, look at its drive — luxury hulls often push better efficiency at cruise than a loaded courier. Might be worth letting it lead.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Pike> Pike runs one last scan of the field behind them — the gutted skiffs still dark, no Guild sweep signatures yet — then pulls on his helmet seal and cycles through the airlock to the beacon.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ghost> At the beacon, Pike unclips his tether and floats clear with his hardsuit and scanner packed tight. Ghost transfers his half of the agreed split details to Pike's link — the deal closed, salvage split honored, claim ID already logged under the Guild filing.\n\nPike: [gravelly, over comms] Deal's done, pilot. Clean work. Ping me when you've stamped that yacht's papers — I know buyers who'll want a look at that cold-chain cargo. Fly safe.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ghost> Pike's mag-boots catch the beacon's rail and he's gone, drifting toward the waiting shuttle lane. Ghost pulls the convoy back together — Vesper Nine, two drones, chrome yacht — and plots for the Ninefold Exchange.\n\nAutomated Steward: [calmly] Captain, while you're in transit — I can prepare the guest quarters and calibrate environmental controls for your arrival. Shall I also queue the re-registration paperwork for the port office at Ninefold?\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ghost> Ghost leans back in the pilot seat as the fold corridor opens, watching the registry summary scroll across his board — the yacht's certificate, the drones' ownership filings, the Carrow claim, all stacked in one place.\n\nNarrator: <arrival> The corridor spits them out under the Ninefold Exchange's approach lights — nine habitat drums ringing a polished finance core, traffic streams threading between towers, dock chatter filling the channels. The Public Concourse level glows through the viewports: service desks, clinics, restaurant fronts, and a steady current of staff and traders moving between the tower entrances.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ghost> Ghost brings the Vesper Nine into a visitor berth on the concourse ring, the chrome yacht settling neatly beside it on the steward's own guidance, both drones tucking into a holding pattern overhead. A berth clerk waves them in, already calling up the mooring fees on her console.",
