in autonomy. Soren and Ghost meet on the Docking Spine to get tea at the Market Ring, where Soren asks Ghost why he flies a courier instead of working manual cargo labor.\n\nVessel Ledger:\n*Lilt*: Wren courier, condition unknown, berth at Docking Spine, owner/captain Ilya Soren, command access Soren, liens present, crew unknown, cargo small urgent freight, fuel unknown, systems unknown.\nGhost and Captain Ilya Soren walk from the Docking Spine to the Market Ring, where Soren buys teas from a stall keeper named Kess. Ghost states that the *Vesper Nine* costs more than it earns and that he owes 1,200 credits in five days. Soren offers Ghost a wreck assessment job past the Ninefold corridor paid by the Guild upon scan delivery.\n\nVessel Ledger:\n*Lilt*: Wren courier, condition unknown, berth at Docking Spine, owner/captain Ilya Soren, command access Soren, liens present, crew unknown, cargo small urgent freight, fuel unknown, systems unknown.\n*Vesper Nine*: Hull class unknown, condition unknown, berth unknown, owner Ghost, command access Ghost, liens unknown, crew unknown, cargo unknown, fuel unknown, systems unknown.\nGhost agrees to take the Ninefold job after Captain Ilya Soren explains she declined it due to low scan fees, fuel costs, and schedule conflicts. Soren accepts a promise from Ghost to discuss future collaborations if the salvage is profitable before she departs for her berth. Kess asks Ghost if he wants a paid tea refill or is leaving.\n\nVessel Ledger:\n*Lilt*: Wren courier, condition unknown, berth at Docking Spine, owner/captain Ilya Soren, command access Soren, liens present, crew unknown, cargo small urgent freight, fuel unknown, systems unknown.\n*Vesper Nine*: Hull class unknown, condition unknown, berth unknown, owner Ghost, command access Ghost, liens unknown, crew unknown, cargo unknown, fuel unknown, systems unknown.\nGhost pays Kess 60 credits for a tea thermos in the Brasse Station Market Ring. At a public kiosk, Ghost accepts an 800-credit Guild contract for a sensor sweep of the Ninefold corridor, a route requiring two fold legs and 14 hours each way. Ghost visits Daret, who offers a passive signal dampener for 1,200 credits or a hardened signal filter for 2,600 credits, or a bundle of both for 3,400 credits including overnight installation. Ghost remains at Daret's stall to decide.\nAt the Brasse Station Market Ring, Ghost paid Daret 3,000 credits for a passive signal dampener with clamps and a hardened signal filter. Ghost traveled to the Docking Spine, boarded the Vesper Nine, and installed both units according to Daret's instructions. After confirming the systems operate without noise spikes, Ghost logged fuel reserves at just under two-thirds of a tank and reviewed an 800-credit job posting for a debris field scan in the Ninefold corridor.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine; Hull Class: [Not specified]; Condition: Systems green; Berth: In collar; Owner: Ghost; Command Access: Ghost; Liens: None; Crew: None; Cargo: None; Fuel: <2/3 tank; Installed Systems: Passive signal dampener, hardened signal filter.\nGhost paid 210 credits for fuel, leaving him with 1,730 credits. Pike approached Ghost at the Vesper Nine and proposed a partnership where Ghost keeps the 800-credit scan fee and receives first pick of a split of salvaged cybernetics from an Orison Combine freighter in exchange for pilot services and a discreet ship. Ghost and Pike moved to slip 14-C, where Pike noted the ship's signal dampener and filter and presented an image of the target hull.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine; Hull Class: [Not specified]; Condition: Systems green; Berth: Slip 14-C; Owner: Ghost; Command Access: Ghost; Liens: None; Crew: None; Cargo: None; Fuel: Full; Installed Systems: Passive signal dampener, hardened signal filter.\n\nConfirmed Fact: Pike identified Ghost as the contractor for the Ninefold scan.\nCharacter Belief: Pike believes the signal dampener and filter will prevent fold noise from interfering with sensor returns.\nRumor: An Orison Combine freighter in the field contains unmanifested cybernetics.\n\nLast Unresolved Choice: Ghost must decide whether to fly solo or partner with Pike.\nGhost and Pike depart Brasse Station aboard the Vesper Nine to salvage an 800-tonne Orison Combine Carrow-class cargo hauler containing industrial sealants and machine parts. Ghost agrees to Pike's salvage split and the plan to file a claim after recovery, provided he can claim the vessel if it is flyable. Thirteen kilometers out, Grak offers Ghost a damaged civilian shield generator in exchange for water canisters and a signal booster while reporting increased fold noise.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine, [Hull Class: Not Specified], Condition: [Not Specified], Route: Departing Brasse Station toward the Exchange, Owner/Public Identity: Ghost, Command Access: Ghost, Liens: [Not Specified], Crew: Ghost, Pike, Cargo: [Not Specified], Fuel/Ammo: [Not Specified], Installed Systems: [Not Specified].\nGhost and Pike traded two water canisters and a signal booster to Grak for a courier-class shield generator, which Ghost installed on the Vesper Nine. Pike prepared his hardsuit, mag-boots, tether reel, and plasma torch while Ghost piloted the ship toward the corridor mouth. Ghost confirmed shifted debris and flat fold noise, deciding to proceed with the plotted entry window.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine, [Hull Class: Not Specified], Condition: [Not Specified], Route: Departing Brasse Station, Owner/Public Identity: Ghost, Command Access: Ghost, Liens: [Not Specified], Crew: Ghost, Pike, Cargo: None, Fuel/Ammo: [Not Specified], Installed Systems: Courier-class shield generator.\nGhost pilots the Vesper Nine to the Ninefold side, where he and Pike locate the wreckage of the Carrow freighter. Ghost instructs Pike to use passive sensors and visual confirmation before scanning and suiting up for EVA. Ghost prepares to anchor the Vesper Nine at the Carrow's aft cargo bay while Pike prepares a handheld ultrasonic scanner and suits up.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine, [Hull Class: Not Specified], Condition: [Not Specified], Route: Ninefold side, Owner/Public Identity: Ghost, Command Access: Ghost, Liens: [Not Specified], Crew: Ghost, Pike, Cargo: None, Fuel/Ammo: [Not Specified], Installed Systems: Courier-class shield generator.\nPike suits up for EVA and asks Ghost for the anchoring position. Ghost anchors the Vesper Nine to the aft flank of the Carrow via magnetic grapple and completes a Guild job scan. Ghost notes a hairline fracture and frost bloom on the cargo bay doors, suggesting a slow atmospheric bleed; Pike states he will rely on his torch and suit over the doors.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine, [Hull Class: Not Specified], Condition: [Not Specified], Route: Ninefold side, Owner/Public Identity: Ghost, Command Access: Ghost, Liens: [Not Specified], Crew: Ghost, Pike, Cargo: None, Fuel/Ammo: [Not Specified], Installed Systems: Courier-class shield generator.\nGhost suits up and jacks his Intrusion Deck into the console. He discovers the freighter has no active security and residual power in the aft section, allowing him to tag door controllers, note pressure readings in aft compartments, and copy a log fragment. The log confirms a cargo seal on bay three but ends abruptly during a power fluctuation. Pike, sealed in his suit and tethered at the airlock, asks Ghost whether to hit the port seam by the fracture or the starboard door.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine, [Hull Class: Not Specified], Condition: [Not Specified], Route: Ninefold side, Owner/Public Identity: Ghost, Command Access: Ghost, Liens: [Not Specified], Crew: Ghost, Pike, Cargo: None, Fuel/Ammo: [Not Specified], Installed Systems: Courier-class shield generator.\nPike decides to cut the starboard door to avoid risking a pressure vent and cargo shift at the port fracture. He instructs Ghost to hold the grapple and keep the tether clear of the fracture zone. Pike identifies the vessel's frame as a write-off due to a sheared spine and dead transponder, and Ghost agrees to focus solely on the cargo. Ghost will monitor pressure readings while Pike prepares his torch to exit on Ghost's mark.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine, [Hull Class: Not Specified], Condition: [Not Specified], Route: Ninefold side, Owner/Public Identity: Ghost, Command Access: Ghost, Liens: [Not Specified], Crew: Ghost, Pike, Cargo: None, Fuel/Ammo: [Not Specified], Installed Systems: Courier-class shield generator.\nGhost used the freighter's residual bus to tag 800 tonnes of cargo under his claim ID, though he noted that a formal Guild filing within seventy-two hours is required to override the external Combine registry. Ghost mapped the freighter, confirming bay three is sealed by the starboard door while bays one, two, and the fore section are open to vacuum or stripped. Pike confirmed his torch pressure is stable and requested Ghost confirm the tether is clear of the port fracture zone before he exits the airlock.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine, [Hull Class: Not Specified], Condition: [Not Specified], Route: Ninefold side, Owner/Public Identity: Ghost, Command Access: Ghost, Liens: [Not Specified], Crew: Ghost, Pike, Cargo: None, Fuel/Ammo: [Not Specified], Installed Systems: Courier-class shield generator.\nGhost discovered a self-powered, refrigerated cargo seal node cycling behind bay three's bulkhead that resists remote queries. Ghost confirmed Vesper Nine's systems are nominal, fuel is under two-thirds, and successfully queued a preliminary Guild claim for the 800 tonnes of cargo after correcting a timestamp discrepancy. Pike exited the airlock and began cutting the starboard cargo door's hinge side with his torch.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine, [Hull Class: Not Specified], Condition: [Not Specified], Route: Ninefold side, Owner/Public Identity: Ghost, Command Access: Ghost, Liens: [Not Specified], Crew: Ghost, Pike, Cargo: None, Fuel/Ammo: Just under two-thirds fuel, Installed Systems: Courier-class shield generator.\nGhost completed and transmitted the Guild scan package, locking in a seventy-two-hour claim for the 800 tonnes of cargo. Ghost exited the airlock and joined Pike at the starboard door, where Pike has cut through one-third of the hinge side. Pike suggested investigating the self-powered node behind bay three's bulkhead while the door remains sealed. Ghost located the corresponding maintenance panel, noting it is a standard service hatch with intact screws and no external power feed.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine, [Hull Class: Not Specified], Condition: [Not Specified], Route: Ninefold side, Owner/Public Identity: Ghost, Command Access: Ghost, Liens: [Not Specified], Crew: Ghost, Pike, Cargo: None, Fuel/Ammo: Just under two-thirds fuel, Installed Systems: Courier-class shield generator.\nGhost and Pike agree to prioritize high-value goods for loading onto the Vesper Nine, maintaining their cargo split. Ghost removes the maintenance panel to reveal an Orison Combine cold-chain cargo canister (Lot 44-C) marked with a medical cross. The unit is currently holding a temperature of minus forty with sixty-one percent cell reserve. Pike identifies the canister as live medical-grade cargo that must be retrieved immediately.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine, [Hull Class: Not Specified], Condition: [Not Specified], Route: Ninefold side, Owner/Public Identity: Ghost, Command Access: Ghost, Liens: [Not Specified], Crew: Ghost, Pike, Cargo: None, Fuel/Ammo: Just under two-thirds fuel, Installed Systems: Courier-class shield generator.\n\n**Latest Story - Tick 46 (editable with rewriteLastStory)**:\nGhost: [flatly] Yeah. Eight hundred tons of cargo's mine — that'll pay good credit once it's shipped. But for now, let's focus on what goods you want out of it and get them loaded on my ship. Also, lemme go have a look at that cycle.\n\nPike: [gravelly] That refrigerated node's been bugging me since you flagged it. Could be a cold-chain medical shipment, could 