it Guild contract for a sensor sweep of the Ninefold corridor, a route requiring two fold legs and 14 hours each way. Ghost visits Daret, who offers a passive signal dampener for 1,200 credits or a hardened signal filter for 2,600 credits, or a bundle of both for 3,400 credits including overnight installation. Ghost remains at Daret's stall to decide.\nAt the Brasse Station Market Ring, Ghost paid Daret 3,000 credits for a passive signal dampener with clamps and a hardened signal filter. Ghost traveled to the Docking Spine, boarded the Vesper Nine, and installed both units according to Daret's instructions. After confirming the systems operate without noise spikes, Ghost logged fuel reserves at just under two-thirds of a tank and reviewed an 800-credit job posting for a debris field scan in the Ninefold corridor.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine; Hull Class: [Not specified]; Condition: Systems green; Berth: In collar; Owner: Ghost; Command Access: Ghost; Liens: None; Crew: None; Cargo: None; Fuel: <2/3 tank; Installed Systems: Passive signal dampener, hardened signal filter.\nGhost paid 210 credits for fuel, leaving him with 1,730 credits. Pike approached Ghost at the Vesper Nine and proposed a partnership where Ghost keeps the 800-credit scan fee and receives first pick of a split of salvaged cybernetics from an Orison Combine freighter in exchange for pilot services and a discreet ship. Ghost and Pike moved to slip 14-C, where Pike noted the ship's signal dampener and filter and presented an image of the target hull.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine; Hull Class: [Not specified]; Condition: Systems green; Berth: Slip 14-C; Owner: Ghost; Command Access: Ghost; Liens: None; Crew: None; Cargo: None; Fuel: Full; Installed Systems: Passive signal dampener, hardened signal filter.\n\nConfirmed Fact: Pike identified Ghost as the contractor for the Ninefold scan.\nCharacter Belief: Pike believes the signal dampener and filter will prevent fold noise from interfering with sensor returns.\nRumor: An Orison Combine freighter in the field contains unmanifested cybernetics.\n\nLast Unresolved Choice: Ghost must decide whether to fly solo or partner with Pike.\nGhost and Pike depart Brasse Station aboard the Vesper Nine to salvage an 800-tonne Orison Combine Carrow-class cargo hauler containing industrial sealants and machine parts. Ghost agrees to Pike's salvage split and the plan to file a claim after recovery, provided he can claim the vessel if it is flyable. Thirteen kilometers out, Grak offers Ghost a damaged civilian shield generator in exchange for water canisters and a signal booster while reporting increased fold noise.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine, [Hull Class: Not Specified], Condition: [Not Specified], Route: Departing Brasse Station toward the Exchange, Owner/Public Identity: Ghost, Command Access: Ghost, Liens: [Not Specified], Crew: Ghost, Pike, Cargo: [Not Specified], Fuel/Ammo: [Not Specified], Installed Systems: [Not Specified].\nGhost and Pike traded two water canisters and a signal booster to Grak for a courier-class shield generator, which Ghost installed on the Vesper Nine. Pike prepared his hardsuit, mag-boots, tether reel, and plasma torch while Ghost piloted the ship toward the corridor mouth. Ghost confirmed shifted debris and flat fold noise, deciding to proceed with the plotted entry window.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine, [Hull Class: Not Specified], Condition: [Not Specified], Route: Departing Brasse Station, Owner/Public Identity: Ghost, Command Access: Ghost, Liens: [Not Specified], Crew: Ghost, Pike, Cargo: None, Fuel/Ammo: [Not Specified], Installed Systems: Courier-class shield generator.\nGhost pilots the Vesper Nine to the Ninefold side, where he and Pike locate the wreckage of the Carrow freighter. Ghost instructs Pike to use passive sensors and visual confirmation before scanning and suiting up for EVA. Ghost prepares to anchor the Vesper Nine at the Carrow's aft cargo bay while Pike prepares a handheld ultrasonic scanner and suits up.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine, [Hull Class: Not Specified], Condition: [Not Specified], Route: Ninefold side, Owner/Public Identity: Ghost, Command Access: Ghost, Liens: [Not Specified], Crew: Ghost, Pike, Cargo: None, Fuel/Ammo: [Not Specified], Installed Systems: Courier-class shield generator.\nGhost anchored the Vesper Nine to the Carrow via magnetic grapple and tagged 800 tonnes of cargo using a log fragment confirming a seal on bay three. Ghost discovered the Carrow has no active security, a dead transponder, and a sheared spine. Pike decided to cut the starboard door to avoid a port-side fracture and requested Ghost confirm the tether is clear before he exits the airlock.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine, [Hull Class: Not Specified], Condition: [Not Specified], Route: Ninefold side, Owner/Public Identity: Ghost, Command Access: Ghost, Liens: [Not Specified], Crew: Ghost, Pike, Cargo: None, Fuel/Ammo: [Not Specified], Installed Systems: Courier-class shield generator.\nGhost locked in a seventy-two-hour Guild claim for 800 tonnes of cargo while Pike began cutting the starboard cargo door of a vessel. Ghost discovered an Orison Combine cold-chain canister containing cryo-preserved surgical biosynths destined for Dr. A. Renholt at Station Vell. Pike insisted that these biosynths be loaded first and kept at temperature to determine a buyer.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine, [Hull Class: Not Specified], Condition: [Not Specified], Route: Ninefold side, Owner/Public Identity: Ghost, Command Access: Ghost, Liens: [Not Specified], Crew: Ghost, Pike, Cargo: None, Fuel/Ammo: Just under two-thirds fuel, Installed Systems: Courier-class shield generator.\nGhost decides to deliver the biosynths to Dr. Renholt to maximize profit and networking. Ghost and Pike load the cryo-canister into the Vesper Nine's center cradle and secure it with mag-clamps. Pike opens the door to bay three, discovering industrial sealants and crated machine parts. Pike confirms no other cold-chain cargo exists and tells Ghost to begin sorting the 800 tonnes of freight for loading.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine, [Hull Class: Not Specified], Condition: [Not Specified], Route: Ninefold side, Owner/Public Identity: Ghost, Command Access: Ghost, Liens: [Not Specified], Crew: Ghost, Pike, Cargo: Lot 44-C biosynths, Fuel/Ammo: Just under two-thirds fuel, Installed Systems: Courier-class shield generator.\nPike and Ghost sort the 800 tonnes of freight in bay three, prioritizing dense sealant bins and then machine parts. Ghost logs bin codes and mass estimates on his wrist display against the Vesper Nine's capacity. Pike identified six sealant bins and a crate of Combine precision tools that he believes is worth inspecting first.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine, [Hull Class: Not Specified], Condition: [Not Specified], Route: Ninefold side, Owner/Public Identity: Ghost, Command Access: Ghost, Liens: [Not Specified], Crew: Ghost, Pike, Cargo: Lot 44-C biosynths, Fuel/Ammo: Just under two-thirds fuel, Installed Systems: Courier-class shield generator.\nPike used an ultrasonic scanner to confirm a crate of Combine precision tooling is high-value and should be prioritized on the manifest. Ghost logged the crate at the top of the sort list, tagging its stencil code and mass. Pike mapped the remaining machine-parts crates and proposed a hauling plan: Ghost will transport light crates while Pike moves the bins. Pike instructed Ghost to monitor the cold-chain unit's cell reserve.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine, [Hull Class: Not Specified], Condition: [Not Specified], Route: Ninefold side, Owner/Public Identity: Ghost, Command Access: Ghost, Liens: [Not Specified], Crew: Ghost, Pike, Cargo: Lot 44-C biosynths, Fuel/Ammo: Just under two-thirds fuel, Installed Systems: Courier-class shield generator.\nGhost confirmed the cold-chain cell reserve is at sixty-one percent. Pike finished scanning the machine-parts row and moved the first sealant bin toward the tether line. Ghost logged the bin transfer and tracked the total mass against the Vesper Nine's capacity.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine, [Hull Class: Not Specified], Condition: [Not Specified], Route: Ninefold side, Owner/Public Identity: Ghost, Command Access: Ghost, Liens: [Not Specified], Crew: Ghost, Pike, Cargo: Lot 44-C biosynths, sealant bin, Fuel/Ammo: Just under two-thirds fuel, Installed Systems: Courier-class shield generator.\nPike locked the first sealant bin to the Vesper Nine's transfer point and freed a second bin in bay three. Pike asked Ghost for the current hold total to determine if a tooling crate would fit.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine, [Hull Class: Not Specified], Condition: [Not Specified], Route: Ninefold side, Owner/Public Identity: Ghost, Command Access: Ghost, Liens: [Not Specified], Crew: Ghost, Pike, Cargo: Lot 44-C biosynths, two sealant bins, Fuel/Ammo: Just under two-thirds fuel, Installed Systems: Courier-class shield generator.\nGhost checked the Vesper Nine's hold totals on his wrist display. Pike stated that six sealant bins and the tooling crate would put the ship near its weight limit. Pike asked Ghost for the specific capacity number to determine which items must be left behind.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine, [Hull Class: Not Specified], Condition: [Not Specified], Route: Ninefold side, Owner/Public Identity: Ghost, Command Access: Ghost, Liens: [Not Specified], Crew: Ghost, Pike, Cargo: Lot 44-C biosynths, two sealant bins, Fuel/Ammo: Just under two-thirds fuel, Installed Systems: Courier-class shield generator.\nGhost calculated that the Vesper Nine has room for two additional sealant bins and the tooling crate, requiring the machine-parts crates and final two bins to be left behind. Pike agreed to this cut and transferred a third sealant bin to the ship. Pike instructed Ghost to prepare the tooling crate to be loaded last to prevent damage.\n\nVessel Ledger: Vesper Nine, [Hull Class: Not Specified], Condition: [Not Specified